{
  "name": "slowworm",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/snakes.py): the SLOW WORM, Anguis fragilis, a LEGLESS LIZARD 42 cm long and 1.3 cm thick, round and the same girth from the head nearly to the tail's end (the tail half of it, ending blunt); a small lizard's head no wider than the body, no neck, the snout short and rounded, small eyes WITH EYELIDS, a short notched tongue; SMOOTH GLOSSY scales in rows (row scales, wet), bronze-copper above; the female with a thin dark line down the spine and dark flanks and belly, the male plain grey-bronze, some with blue spots; the young gold above, black below. A slow sinuous crawl.",
